{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "status": "passed full build, root lint and transitive axiom audit; both whole thresholds remain open",
  "scope": "Independent all-count cross-cutoff estimate: |Q(R,S)|<=C/(4+|log R-log S|)^2 for all positive cutoffs, with one unevaluated constant. For fixed log spacing h>0, the finite Suzuki Schur inequality gives a joint signed quadratic at most E_h*sum a_i^2, with no period-count factor. The actual integer interval mean is at most E_h*(X-Y)*sum a_i^2+(sum |a_i|*R_i)^2. A sharper version replaces the finite-error square by (sum_d |mu(d)*sum_(i:d<=R_i) a_i|)^2, combining cutoff coefficients before the absolute value. Both signed sides preserve arbitrary population selections and a common real weight. The cutoffSlope bridge retains strict endpoints R_i<exp(D_i)<=R_i+1. The coefficient family a_i is fixed across labels; arbitrary a_i(n) is not covered. The actual prime-period coefficient variation, matching cutoff correction, weight energy and combined finite floor error remain unpaid at source scale. The optional alternating Gram probe is not a certificate or a masked-carrier estimate. Do not count paid sectors twice. Both whole -79/1000 floor and 3/2 ceiling remain open; no zero exclusion or RH claim.",
